Z||000006||Smoooooth GT||12-16-2001||02:21 AM||||Hmmm...  I thought that ALL the Pace car's were...umm..  WHITE????? <P>Thank's for the pic's !! Too bad that the glass was sooo scratched up...   <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vroom_5.gif">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                <BR>      <P> <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||12-16-2001||02:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> <BR>One bit of bad news about the Pace Car. I inspected the wheels & found that yes Centerline made them but.... The flat center part of the wheel looks like a cover. Its not a complete solid wheel. If you look in the holes you can see another wheel behind it..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's funny that you bring this up because I was just talking to Paul today about this same subject! He found out that the chrome part is just a wheel cover and it fits over a steel 16 inch wheel.<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||G-Nasty||12-16-2001||04:15 AM||||What are you InsanE??! aRE yOU guys...Jessica Fletcher meets Matlock? This is typical fiero antics-So somebody stole the REAL INDY and left this raggedy ole' brown n white plastic thing with cheap hubcaps...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||12-16-2001||04:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by G-Nasty:<BR><B>What are you InsanE??! aRE yOU guys...Jessica Fletcher meets Matlock? This is typical fiero antics-So somebody stole the REAL INDY and left this raggedy ole' brown n white plastic thing with cheap hubcaps...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope not insane the real Indy car had the same wheel covers on it and the interior is supposedly just like a regular Fiero interior<BR>and not like the Pace car replicas that the public could buy. The replicas had the red and white interior while the real deal Indy cars just had regular grey interior.<BR>The guy that Paul got this info from actually saw the real Indy cars while they were on the track and he collects a lot of indy stuff.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000010||T-top Fiero||12-16-2001||11:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B> Nope not insane the real Indy car had the same wheel covers on it and the interior is supposedly just like a regular Fiero interior<BR>and not like the Pace car replicas that the public could buy. The replicas had the red and white interior while the real deal Indy cars just had regular grey interior.<BR>The guy that Paul got this info from actually saw the real Indy cars while they were on the track and he collects a lot of indy stuff.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That info about the interiors of the real Indy pace cars is wrong. Of the three cars made for the race, two of them had the gray and red interior (just like the replicas) and the other one had the tan/brown interior with the suede and fleece insert seats. The reason the one had the tan/brown interior is because John Callies (the driver) liked that interior better.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Smoooooth GT||12-16-2001||12:17 PM||||I thought that ALL Pace Car's were White???? Anyone know different??<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vroom_5.gif">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                <BR>      <P> <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Hartz||12-16-2001||12:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B>I thought that ALL Pace Car's were White???? Anyone know different??<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't confuse the Indy 500 pace cars with the PPG pace cars.  Yes, I think all Indy pace cars were white.  PPG cars were a variety of colors over the years.<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000013||Haze_Performance||12-16-2001||01:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B>I thought that ALL Pace Car's were White???? Anyone know different??<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>All the Indy 500 cars were White with Silver gfx. Now I've seen MANY colors on the PPG Fiero Pace Cars..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000014||Smoooooth GT||12-16-2001||02:13 PM||||Duh.... I did confuse the two. Thank's for clarifying(sp?) the difference between the two!! <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vroom_5.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                 <BR>      <P> <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
