Z||000025||Dave Gunsul||12-16-2001||11:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> Does he know any other info about it?? Is there any of these wheels or covers around anymore??  <P>Thanks   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not sure you'd have to ask him. The guy that he learned this info from is some kind of Indy Fiero expert though so you might want to talk to Paul and see if he has anything or any info that you'd be interested in because he told me that the guy is wanting to get rid of some of his Indy stuff.<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000026||kslish||12-17-2001||01:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Now, for a really stupid question...what is PPG?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>PPG stands for Pittsburgh Plate Glass.  Based in Pittsburgh, PA, they are a major manufacturer of auto and house glass, paints and coatings, fiberglass and some specialty chemicals.<P>And the only reason I know this is because their headquarters are located about 3 miles from my house....<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Reality||12-17-2001||06:27 AM||||Not the one i was thinking of, but still a nice addition to the picture collection. The one I heard about looked just like the indy car cept instead of red accents it had blue and said PPG on it?? ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Oreif||12-17-2001||08:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokid87:<BR><B>The PPG Pace car is similar to the Indy But paced a different kind of racing?  What class did it pace?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They paced a few different races. Usually<BR>IMSA GTU class races. I do remember one of the fastback ones paced a GTP race when they brought out the Spice/Entac race car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Fierokid87||12-17-2001||10:02 AM||||That Blue Pace car Im pretty sure is not an 89 Fiero.  It looks similar but the side scoop does not run the whole length of the door.  And the molding is 86-88 rounded molding.  And the rocker panels sport the GT/SE ground FX<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000030||Fie Ro||12-17-2001||10:50 AM||||I really like the nose of the blue PPG car<P>does anyone make them??????||||reg||6
Z||000031||NIFE [PaulV]||12-17-2001||12:41 PM||||The original 3 "track" pace cars all had the Fiero tan interior!||||reg||1
Z||000032||NIFE [PaulV]||12-17-2001||12:49 PM||||A few other bits of info:<BR>The 3 "track" pace cars had a "Centerline Wheel" look by using a wheel cover over a regular steel wheel. I believe they were 16" wheels.No one knows where there might be a replica of these covers.<P>Museum car....we did a very lenghly story on this car about 3-4 years ago. I was able to get into the "glass" booth at the museum after hours with a professional photogropher. We took lots of pictures, and interviewed several people at the museum and GM about the car. I even tracked down John Callies to talk about the car. If anyone is interested, I would be glad to post the article here.<BR>We also just completed a short article about the PPG pace cars, along with a picture of a group of these cars on a track. The article with a picture will be in our Jan/Feb NIFE newsletter. Not a lot of info on these cars.||||reg||1
