Z||000052||Haze_Performance||12-17-2001||11:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>Do you doubt it can be done?<P>Behold!!!  I even took the liberty of removing the gas tanks.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That took me all of 5 minutes.  So to me, it was a valid possibility.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not to bad BUT!!!!! What about the "Goodyear Eagle GT" on the tires of the red one... LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000053||Pyric||12-17-2001||11:37 PM||||I was going to fix that but I figured it wasn't that legible.  Besides, that would have taken a whole 30 seconds more.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ppg4.jpg"> <P>So here. The tires are fixed and I added an intake to the red one as well as tinting the windows.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000054||kslish||12-18-2001||04:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B>This car belonged (belongs?) to Pontiac.  I remember the story being that this was the first driveable, pre-production prototype.  Not the first production car (which I think I read somewhere was white) but rather the first prototype - and they hadn't decided on putting in the air intake yet.  I guess that came later.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've got a video that talks about the prototype.  Apparently, on the original prototype mule, the air intake was underneath the car, but that sucked in too much durt and dust into the air cleaner housing so they made the side intake as sort of a late design afterthought to fix the problem. <BR> <BR>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000055||chester||12-18-2001||08:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> <BR>The sign behind the car says that the original Indy 500 Pace Car is in the Indy 500 Museum in Indianapolis. I thought some said it wasn't there?? I'm not sure. I'm going to call the Museum Monday & ask them.. (One more road trip)  <P><BR>One bit of bad news about the Pace Car. I inspected the wheels & found that yes Centerline made them but.... The flat center part of the wheel looks like a cover. Its not a complete solid wheel. If you look in the holes you can see another wheel behind it..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P><BR>P.S. Tire size:<BR>Front - GoodYear VR50 225/50/ZR16<BR>Rear - GoodYear VR50 255/50ZR16<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I called Centerline about those rims.  They told me that only 2 or 3 (guy wasn't sure) sets were ever made just for the Indy pace car and then the tooling was destroyed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> . Maybe those are repros of the originals?<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000056||Swany||12-18-2001||12:57 PM||||well, either way. that is one sweet looking nose.. (on the blue ppg car) wish we had a better view of it. <P>I'd like to find a facia/nose like that available for purchase. <P>the nose on my gt is cracked, and when I replace it, it would be cool to replace it with something like that. :-)<p>[This message has been edited by Swany (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000057||Haze_Performance||12-18-2001||01:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B> I called Centerline about those rims.  They told me that only 2 or 3 (guy wasn't sure) sets were ever made just for the Indy pace car and then the tooling was destroyed   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> . Maybe those are repros of the originals?<P>Rob D.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wouldn't think that they would be repros.. The sign behind the car says that the car was donated to the museum by GM. I don't think they would use repros.. (I guess anything could happen thou...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<BR>||||reg||5
